<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">inventory</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">inventory</ansi> command shows your equipment and backpack
contents.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">inventory</ansi>             Show all equipment and carried items.
  <ansi fg="command">inventory wood</ansi>         Filter to items with "wood" in the name.
  <ansi fg="command">inventory wearable</ansi>     Filter to wearable items.
  <ansi fg="command">inventory weapons</ansi>      Filter to weapons.
  <ansi fg="command">inventory potions</ansi>      Filter to potions.

Identical items are stacked together with a count, for example:
<ansi fg="itemname">iron ingot</ansi> <ansi fg="uses-left">(x5)</ansi> means you are carrying five iron ingots.

Your encumbrance level is shown at the bottom, ranging from
<ansi fg="green">light</ansi> to <ansi fg="magenta-bold">crushed</ansi>. Being overburdened costs extra
stamina to move and reduces your effectiveness in combat. You
can add <ansi fg="magenta">{enc}</ansi> to your prompt to track this at a glance
(see <ansi fg="command">help set prompt</ansi>).

If you have a component bag equipped, crafting materials stored in
it appear in a separate Components section at the bottom of your
inventory. Use <ansi fg="command">sort</ansi> to move loose materials from your
backpack into the bag.

To learn more about an item's properties, use the
<ansi fg="spellname">identify</ansi> spell or visit a merchant and
use <ansi fg="command">appraise</ansi>.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help identify</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help appraise</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help item-names</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help sort</ansi>

